---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import styles from '../styles/legal.module.css';
---

<Layout
  title="WitrQuran Is Open Source | WitrQuran"
  description="WitrQuran is an open source Quran listening platform built to make listening to the Quran simple, fast, and accessible to everyone."
>
  <div class={styles.pageContainer}>
    <nav class={styles.breadcrumb} aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span>Open Source</span>
    </nav>

    <header class={styles.header}>
      <h1 class={styles.title}>WitrQuran Is Open Source</h1>
    </header>

    <div class={styles.content}>
      <p>WitrQuran is an open source Quran listening platform built with one simple goal</p>

      <p><strong>Make listening to the Quran simple fast and accessible to everyone</strong></p>

      <p>The Quran is the Book of Almighty Allah SWT</p>

      <p>WitrQuran does not create or claim ownership of the Quran</p>

      <p>We simply built a tool to make listening to it easier for everyone by the will of Allah SWT</p>

      <h2>Fully Open Source</h2>

      <p>The source code of WitrQuran is publicly available on GitHub</p>

      <p>Anyone can inspect the code understand how the platform works report issues suggest improvements or contribute to the project</p>

      <p>You do not have to simply trust us</p>

      <p><strong>You can verify it yourself</strong></p>

      <h3>View the Source Code</h3>

      <p><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk/WitrQuran?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View WitrQuran on GitHub</a></p>

      <h3>View Faruk's GitHub</h3>

      <p><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Faruk's GitHub Profile</a></p>

      <h2>MIT License</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran is released under the <strong>MIT License</strong></p>

      <p>The MIT License allows people to use copy modify merge publish distribute sublicense and sell copies of the software subject to the conditions of the license</p>

      <p>You can read the complete license directly in the repository</p>

      <p><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk/WitrQuran/blob/main/LICENSE?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the MIT License</a></p>

      <h2>Built in Public</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran is not a closed platform where the underlying software is hidden from its users</p>

      <p>The source code is available publicly so developers and users can inspect the project and understand how it is built</p>

      <p>This also means that improvements can come from the wider community</p>

      <h2>Contributions Are Welcome</h2>

      <p>If you are a developer and want to help improve WitrQuran you are welcome to contribute</p>

      <p>You can</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Report bugs</li>
        <li>Suggest improvements</li>
        <li>Open issues</li>
        <li>Submit pull requests</li>
        <li>Improve the code</li>
        <li>Help make the listening experience better</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Please review the repository before contributing</p>

      <p><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk/WitrQuran?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Contribute on GitHub</a></p>

      <h2>Built With Open Source Technology</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran is built using modern web technologies including</p>

      <p><strong>Astro</strong></p>

      <p><strong>Cloudflare</strong></p>

      <p><strong>Vercel</strong></p>

      <p>The project itself remains publicly inspectable through its GitHub repository</p>

      <h2>Why Open Source</h2>

      <p>We believe transparency is valuable</p>

      <p>Making the code public allows people to see how WitrQuran works rather than asking them to blindly trust a platform</p>

      <p>It also gives developers an opportunity to learn from the project and contribute improvements</p>

      <h2>Created by Faruk</h2>

      <p>WitrQuran was created by <strong>Md Faruk Abdulla</strong></p>

      <p>Faruk built the platform to make Quran listening simpler and more accessible</p>

      <p>The Quran belongs to Almighty Allah SWT</p>

      <p>The work here is simply the creation of a tool to make listening easier by the will of Allah SWT</p>

      <h2>Stay Connected</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.instagram.com/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://x.com/witrfaruk?utm_source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">X</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p>If you find an issue or have an idea that could improve WitrQuran you can contribute through the public repository</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
